## Phaser-Specific Notes

1. Use Phaser's built-in audio formats and fallbacks:
   ```typescript
   // Provide multiple formats for cross-browser compatibility
   this.load.audio('explosion', [
     'assets/audio/explosion.ogg', // Smaller file size, preferred
     'assets/audio/explosion.mp3'  // Wider compatibility
   ]);
   ```

2. Take advantage of Phaser's sound manager for global control:
   ```typescript
   // Global mute
   this.sound.mute = true;
   
   // Global volume
   this.sound.volume = 0.5;
   
   // Pause all sounds
   this.sound.pauseAll();
   
   // Resume all sounds
   this.sound.resumeAll();
   ```

3. Use Phaser's built-in audio features for advanced control:
   ```typescript
   const sound = this.sound.add('effect', {
     volume: 0.5,
     rate: 1.0,
     detune: 0,
     seek: 0,
     loop: false,
     delay: 0
   });
   
   // Change playback rate on the fly (pitch shift)
   sound.setRate(1.5);
   
   // Set spatial position for stereo panning
   sound.setPan(-1.0); // Left speaker
   ```

4. Use Phaser's event system for audio synchronization:
   ```typescript
   // React to audio events
   sound.once('complete', () => {
     // Do something when sound finishes
   });
   
   // Create timed gameplay events
   const music = this.sound.add('music');
   music.play();
   
   music.once('looped', () => {
     // Trigger event at end of music loop
     this.spawnBoss();
   });
   ```

5. Use markers for sprite sheets of audio:
   ```typescript
   // Add multiple sound effects within one audio file
   const sfx = this.sound.add('sfx_sprite');
   
   // Define markers for different parts of the audio file
   sfx.addMarker({
     name: 'jump',
     start: 0,
     duration: 0.5
   });
   
   sfx.addMarker({
     name: 'coin',
     start: 0.5,
     duration: 0.25
   });
   
   // Play specific marker
   sfx.play('jump');
   